<title>PERU: Peru says negotiating six hydrocarbon contracts.</title>
<headline>Peru says negotiating six hydrocarbon contracts.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>State oil licensing agent Perupetro is negotiating six exploration and development contracts for hydrocarbon fields with various international firms and one major local company, an Energy and Mines ministry source said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The six contracts are in full negotiation,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He named the companies involved as U.S. companies Coastal and Atlantic Richfield Company ; Anglo-Dutch group Royal Dutch/Shell Group ; Argentina's Pluspetrol; Britain's Enterprise Oil, and Peru's Buenaventura Ingenieros.</p>
<p>Perupetro has signed 36 contracts since it started offering exploration licenses to private companies four years ago.</p>
<p>(( -- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
